From: cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] masks: cover the whole SSID space, not 1.3% of it

The range table diag-router ships covers 647 SSIDs out of 49252, 1.3%, with a
gap of 38735 consecutive ones between 10417 and 49151. Subsystems whose SSID
falls in a gap receive no mask and therefore never emit.

While looking for why the modem says nothing about RF: MCPM and RFLM fall
outside the table. It is replaced by a complete tiling of 200 ranges of 256
SSIDs each. Each mask takes 1 KB, well below the maximum packet size the modem
advertises (32 KB).

